        "titolo_orig": "Brazil bowler Cardoso takes 9 Lesotho wickets in record-breaking T20 win",
        "testo_it": "Brasile: bowler Cardoso compie impresa nel cricket, 9 wicket in una partita T20.",
        "priorita": "Bassa",
        "id_gruppo": 15,
        "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/sports/2026/4/9/brazil-bowler-cardoso-takes-9-lesotho-wickets-in-record-breaking-t20-win?traffic_source=rss",
        "orario": "16:33",
        "timestamp": 1775745237,
        "contenuto_esteso": "By Kevin Hand Published On 9 Apr 2026 9 Apr 2026 Brazil are the unlikely candidates to have claimed two cricket records as one of their bowlers took a record nine wickets – including five in a row – in their 189-run T20 Women’s International victory against Lesotho in Botswana. Having won the toss on Thursday, at the BCA Kalahari Women’s T20 International Tournament, Brazil posted a daunting 202-8 with wicketkeeper Monnike Machado hitting 69 off 41. Recommended Stories list of 4 items list 1 of 4 Eritrea’s AFCON place in doubt after players disappear in South Africa list 2 of 4 Bosnian ball boy hailed as hero after hiding Italian goalkeeper’s notes list 3 of 4 CAF president visits Dakar following AFCON trophy reversal list 4 of 4 World Athletics postpones Doha Diamond League due to player safety concerns end of list The fun, for the Brazilians, was only just beginning, though, as Laura Cardoso claimed a hat-trick with the last three deliveries of her first over – the second of the Lesotho innings – to set in motion the incredible feat that eventually saw the Africans bowled out for 13. The 21-year-old then continued her wicket-taking achievement with a Women’s T20 International first of five dismissals in a row as she struck with the first two balls of her second over. This was all part of claiming the first nine Lesotho wickets to fall, but being denied the chance to take all 10 after a change of bowling following her third over. Her final wicket was Ret’sepile Limema, who fell to the fifth ball of the fifth over, with Cardoso replaced for the following over at that end. Her nine wickets, nevertheless, is the best return in either men’s or women’s T20 internationals. The right-arm seamer did, indeed, come close to another hat-trick, when she claimed wickets with the last two balls of her second over, which itself totalled four victims. Cardoso replaces Indonesia’s Rohmalia Rohmalia at the top of the Women’s T20 best bowling rankings, as she finished with figures of 3-2-4-9. Advertisement Rohmalia had claimed seven wickets in 2024 in a match against Mongolia in Bali. Only three other women have claimed seven in a T20 international. The previous record for the number of wickets in consecutive deliveries was four, and was jointly held with the most prominent occasion being when Shakera Selman pulled off the feat for the West Indies against Pakistan in 2018. Although a huge winning margin, Brazil’s overall win does not compare with Argentina’s record after they beat Chile by 364 runs in 2023. The Argentinians had struck 427-1 to set up their victory. Lesotho’s part in the record extends to no further than Cardoso’s haul, with the record lowest total belonging to Mali, who were bowled out for 6 in 2019 by Rwanda. Brazil, ‌who lead the six-team tournament with five straight wins, play ‌Mozambique ‌on Friday."
